{"t": 178.6, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Bridge_Zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed S4, S5, and S6 due to insufficient voltage (power extraction) and S3 due to overvoltage. I am implementing a Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) topology. By adding an inductor and a switch across the piezo that closes at the voltage extrema, the charge on the piezo capacitor Cp is inverted each half-cycle, significantly increasing the energy extracted. A full-bridge rectifier directs this energy to the storage capacitor, and a DZ33 Zener diode clamps the output voltage to 3.3V to satisfy the vmax <= 3.6V constraint for S3.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Bridge_Zener", "rationale": "The reference FBR failed S4, S5, and S6 due to insufficient voltage (power extraction) and S3 due to overvoltage. I am implementing a Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor (SSHI) topology. By adding an inductor and a switch across the piezo that closes at the voltage extrema, the charge on the piezo capacitor Cp is inverted each half-cycle, significantly increasing the energy extracted. A full-bridge rectifier directs this energy to the storage capacitor, and a DZ33 Zener diode clamps the output voltage to 3.3V to satisfy the vmax <= 3.6V constraint for S3.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.01}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D5", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}]}}
